# Keeps the Docker build context small AND, critically, prevents the host's
# own node_modules (built for the host OS/arch, with pnpm symlinks pointing
# at host-absolute paths like D:/.../node_modules/.pnpm/...) from being
# COPY'd into an image and shadowing the node_modules pnpm installs correctly
# INSIDE each build stage for the container's own OS/arch. Without this, a
# `COPY apps/api apps/api` (etc.) after `pnpm install` silently overwrites a
# perfectly good Linux node_modules with a broken Windows/macOS one.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
.git
.github
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
test-results
data
**/data
*.db
*.db-journal
.env
.env.local
.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
.vscode
.claude
